<script>
import CopyEmail from 'crm/src/contacts/lib/CopyEmail.abide'
import copyEmailSource from 'crm/src/contacts/lib/CopyEmail.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import copyEmailTestSource from 'crm/src/contacts/lib/CopyEmail.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import QuickEdit from 'crm/src/contacts/lib/QuickEdit.abide'
import quickEditSource from 'crm/src/contacts/lib/QuickEdit.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import quickEditTestSource from 'crm/src/contacts/lib/QuickEdit.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }
import ContractDrop from 'crm/src/deals/lib/ContractDrop.abide'
import contractDropSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/ContractDrop.abide' with { type: 'text' }
import contractDropTestSource from 'crm/src/deals/lib/ContractDrop.test.ts' with { type: 'text' }

import Doc from '#src/lib/Doc.abide'
import Example from '#src/lib/Example.abide'
import Registry from '#src/lib/Registry.abide'
import Section from '#src/lib/Section.abide'
import Snippet from '#src/lib/Snippet.abide'
</script>

<Doc>
    <Section title="A panel closes on a press outside it, or on Escape">
        <Example
            id="elements-dismissible"
            title={'`dismissible(onDismiss, { inside })` — closed from outside'}
            summary="A rep opens Ada's quick edit and changes her company. A press anywhere else on the page closes the panel, and so does Escape; the button that opened it closes it too."
            files={{
                'src/contacts/lib/QuickEdit.abide': quickEditSource,
                'src/contacts/lib/QuickEdit.test.ts': quickEditTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <QuickEdit />
        </Example>

        <p>Each helper on this page is a <code>bind:element</code> adaptor, the shape
            <code>observe</code> hands back: a function of the element that hands back what
            stops it. It stops when the element leaves, so a panel under
            <code>{'{#if}'}</code> listens only while it is open. Bind several to one element as
            a list, <code>{'bind:element={[dismissible(close), dropzone(attach)]}'}</code>.</p>

        <p>A press counts as inside the panel and every element <code>inside</code> holds. Hand
            it the button that opens the panel, or its press closes the panel and its click opens
            it again. The press that opened the panel is over before the panel is bound, so it
            never closes what it opened.</p>

        <Snippet source={quickEditSource} path="src/contacts/lib/QuickEdit.abide"
            from={['<form class=']} />

        <p>Panels open at once stack in the order they opened. Escape closes the top one alone,
            and a press closes each one it lands outside, from the top, until the one it lands
            in. So a menu opened from the panel closes first. Escape is skipped where a field
            inside took it for itself with <code>preventDefault</code>. The Escape that closes a
            panel calls it, so a page shortcut on Escape does not run as well. Turn either off
            with <code>{'{ escape: false }'}</code> or <code>{'{ outside: false }'}</code>.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Files dropped on an element, filtered by type">
        <Example
            id="elements-dropzone"
            title={'`dropzone(onFiles, { accept })` — files dropped on a deal'}
            summary="A rep drags the signed contract onto the Ledger audit deal. The box lights up while files hover over it, and only a PDF is attached."
            files={{
                'src/deals/lib/ContractDrop.abide': contractDropSource,
                'src/deals/lib/ContractDrop.test.ts': contractDropTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <ContractDrop />
        </Example>

        <p><code>accept</code> is written the way an <code>{'<input type="file">'}</code>
            writes it: MIME types, <code>image/*</code> wildcards and <code>.pdf</code>
            extensions. Your callback gets the files it takes, and is not called where it takes
            none. The drop is refused its default either way, so a PDF dropped beside the box
            does not open in the tab.</p>

        <p><code>accept</code> also takes a function from the transfer to the files it takes.
            <code>{'accept: imageFiles'}</code> takes the images a model is shown, ready for
            <code>imagePiece</code>. <code>{'{ paste: true }'}</code> takes files pasted into the
            element as a drop, and words pasted alone paste as they always do.
            <code>{'{ multiple: false }'}</code> takes the first file alone.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="A click copies a value, and the element says it did">
        <Example
            id="elements-copy-text"
            title="`copyText(text)` — a contact's email to the clipboard"
            summary="A rep copies Grace's email address to paste into a message. The button reads Copied until the mark wears off."
            files={{
                'src/contacts/lib/CopyEmail.abide': copyEmailSource,
                'src/contacts/lib/CopyEmail.test.ts': copyEmailTestSource,
            }}
        >
            <CopyEmail />
        </Example>

        <p>A click writes the text to the clipboard and puts <code>data-copied</code> on the
            element for <code>copiedFor</code>, 1500 milliseconds by default. The CRM's button
            swaps its word by that attribute alone, with Tailwind's <code>group-data-copied</code>
            variant, so nothing in the script holds whether it copied.</p>

        <Snippet source={copyEmailSource} path="src/contacts/lib/CopyEmail.abide"
            from={['<button class="group"']} />

        <p>Hand <code>copyText</code> a function to copy text that changes, and it is read at
            the click. <code>navigator.clipboard</code> exists only on HTTPS and
            <code>localhost</code>, so a page served over plain HTTP copies through a hidden
            textarea instead.</p>
    </Section>

    <Section title="Styling an element by the attribute a behavior writes">
        <p>None of the three adds a class or a style. Two write a <code>data-</code> attribute
            on the element they are bound to while a state holds, and you style that.</p>

        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Attribute</th><th>Written by</th><th>Present while</th><th>Target it with</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>data-dragging</code></td><td><code>dropzone</code></td><td>files are dragged over the element, its children included</td><td><code>data-dragging:border-signal</code>, or <code>[data-dragging]</code> in a stylesheet</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>data-copied</code></td><td><code>copyText</code></td><td><code>copiedFor</code> milliseconds after a copy lands</td><td><code>data-copied:text-signal</code> on the element, <code>group-data-copied:inline</code> on a child of an element with <code>group</code>, or <code>[data-copied]</code></td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>

        <p><code>dismissible</code> writes nothing: the panel is open while your own value says
            so, and that value is what an <code>{'{#if}'}</code> or a class reads.</p>
    </Section>

    <Registry />
</Doc>
